        "Node name for S&R": "PixaromaInfo"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>HOW TO USE</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>One Run turns every picture in a folder into three social media sizes at once: a square post, a tall post and a story. Each size goes into its own folder, with the original file names.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"folder-v1\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Pick your folder</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ol><li>On <b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma</b>, click <b>Browse</b> and pick your folder, or paste the folder's path into the box.</li><li>Click <b>Pick images</b>, then <b>Select all</b>, or click only the pictures you want. The button shows how many are picked.</li><li>Press <b>Run</b> once. Leave the Run count at <b>1</b>: the node sends every picture through by itself, one after the other.</li></ol><p>\\n\\n</p><p>This workflow opens with <b>no folder picked</b>: choose your own folder, or try it first on the demo folder <b>Products</b> inside the <b>Media Inputs</b> folder that comes with these workflows.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;A folder inside ComfyUI's own <code>input</code> or <code>output</code> folder works straight away. A folder anywhere else works too, but pick it once with <b>Browse</b>: that is how ComfyUI knows you allowed it.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Pictures go through in name order. Name them <code>01_</code>, <code>02_</code> and so on if the order matters.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"gear\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Change the sizes</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li>Type any width and height into a <b>Resize Crop Pixaroma</b> node. It always fills the size completely: it crops the edges, it never stretches and never adds bars.</li><li>The crop is taken from the middle, so keep the subject near the centre of your pictures. A product shot on a plain background works best.</li><li>Need only one size? Click the Save node you do not want and press <b>Ctrl+M</b> to mute it. Its Resize Crop stops running too.</li><li>Need a fourth size? Copy one Resize Crop and its Save node, wire them the same way and give the new Save its own folder name.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"run-timer\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;How long it takes</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>4 pictures in 3 sizes, 12 files, took <b>1.5 s</b> on a 4090. No AI model is used.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"question-mark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Something not working?</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Each button opens the answer on the Pixaroma help page.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/faq/#q-folder-not-approved\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Folder not approved</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/faq/#q-save-other-folder\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Save to your own folder</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/look/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Nodes look different from the video</a></span>&nbsp;</p><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"How to Use\",\"icon\":\"to-do\",\"color\":\"#2a9d8f\"}}"
      ],
